  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). You set a carbon emission scenario and run LOSCAR forward to get pCO2, d13C, pH and CCD trajectories, or you supply proxy pCO2/d13C/pH records and invert them with a TOMS748 root search into an emission history; a LOWESS tool smooths the proxy series first. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
